{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21250 - PROTEIN:5353",
  "verbalization": "Glabrene is implicated in the interaction with ASPC1 through a multi-step pathway involving G-protein coupled receptor 81. The evidence suggests that Glabrene targets G-protein coupled receptor 81, which is subsequently targeted by Trijuganone C and 1,2-Methylenedioxy-4-(1-propenyl)benzene, both of which have a target relationship with ASPC1. This indicates that Glabrene may influence ASPC1 through a series of molecular interactions, potentially via the activation of G-protein coupled receptors. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Glabrene could modulate ASPC1 activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a complex, interconnected relationship between Glabrene and ASPC1, emphasizing the role of receptor signaling in mediating these interactions.",
